<!--
  <sui-status-dot> — SUI port of <ship-status-dot>.
  Colored dot for live/online state indicators with optional pulse animation.

  Prop / event / method parity vs <ship-status-dot>
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Lit                             SUI                     Notes
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  tone (String, 'success')        tone (union, reflect)   ✓
  pulse (Boolean, false)          pulse (bool, reflect)   ✓
  size ('sm'|'md', 'md')          size (union, reflect)   ✓
  label (String, '')              label (string)          ✓
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  (no events)                     (no events)             ✓
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  parts: dot                      part="dot"              ✓
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  reducedMotion mixin             @media prefers-reduced-motion inline   ✓
  toneVars mixin                  :host([tone=...]) inline               ✓
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from the feat/next baseline, parity-gate pass)
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - DELETED the per-component `<theme prop="tone" channels="tone-fg,
    tone-halo-strong, tone-halo-soft">` block. Checked every one of the 8
    tone values against the framework's global contract (packages/sui/
    runtime tones.css TONES_CSS): `tone-fg` is a byte-identical alias match
    (e.g. its `success: success` vs the global's `success: tone-success-fg`
    resolve to the same value — tokens.css defines
    `--tone-success-fg: var(--success)`), and `tone-halo-strong`/
    `tone-halo-soft` are exactly the global `--tone-border`/`--tone-ring`
    channels (same per-tone token names). This is a pure deletion, not a
    value-normalizing swap like the alert/timeline pilots hit — `.dot` now
    reads `bg:tone-fg` and the ring reads `var(--tone-border)`/
    `var(--tone-ring)` directly, zero visual change.
  - Friction worth flagging (not a LANG-GAP, but a token-scale gap): the
    halo ring widths (1.5px / 4.5px / 1px / 3.5px) have no matching step in
    the space scale (which jumps 4px/5px/6px/8px/…, nothing near 1-2px or
    4-5px sub-integer). A prior automated token-routing pass had picked
    `var(--space-1_25)` (5px) and `var(--space-4_5)` (18px) for the 1.5px/
    4.5px rings — a real bug (the "4.5" in the token name was read as a
    space-scale index, not a pixel count, landing 4x too large). Restored
    the literal px values (the compiler's css-token lint only rejects raw
    *colors*, not raw lengths — confirmed empirically) to stay faithful to
    the baseline's fine ring geometry; a design-system fix would add a
    sub-integer space step (or a dedicated halo-ring token) so hairline
    decorative rings like this don't need literal numbers at all.
  - Dot diameter (8px / 6px) and border-radius (50%) already had exact
    token matches (`--icon-size-3xs`, `--space-1_5`, `--radius-full`) from
    the prior pass and are kept as-is.
  - No LANG-GAP: every prop/slot/ARIA rule from the baseline is fully
    expressible on this surface.
-->

<prop name="tone" values="default|primary|info|success|warning|destructive|accent|muted" default="default" reflect />
<prop name="pulse" type="bool" default="false" reflect />
<prop name="size" values="sm|md" default="md" reflect />
<prop name="label" type="string" default="" />

<style>
  :host {
    display: inline-flex;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .dot {
    display: inline-block;
    width: var(--icon-size-3xs);
    height: var(--icon-size-3xs);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1.5px var(--tone-border),
      0 0 0 4.5px var(--tone-ring);
  }
  :host([size='sm']) .dot {
    width: var(--space-1_5);
    height: var(--space-1_5);
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1px var(--tone-border),
      0 0 0 3.5px var(--tone-ring);
  }

  :host([pulse]) .dot { animation: sui-status-dot-pulse 2.5s var(--ease-out) infinite; }
  @keyframes sui-status-dot-pulse {
    0%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); }
    50%      { opacity: 0.82; transform: scale(0.92); }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    :host([pulse]) .dot { animation: none; }
  }
</style>

<span
  class="dot"
  part="dot"
  role={label() ? 'img' : null}
  aria-label={label() || null}
  aria-hidden={label() ? null : 'true'}
  sx="bg:tone-fg"
></span>
